Package: gbpp
Title: Gradient Boosting for Point Processes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Rendi Andria Gita", "Putra", email = "ragita.dev@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Achmad", "Choiruddin", email = "choiruddin@its.ac.id", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Fits gradient boosted point process models to univariate spatial
    point patterns on planar domains and linear networks. Implements
    point-process-specific loss functions including Berman-Turner weighted
    Poisson pseudo-likelihood and logistic likelihood with negative sampling.
    Interfaces with gradient boosting backends including 'xgboost' (Chen and
    Guestrin, 2016 <doi:10.1145/2939672.2939785>), 'lightgbm' (Ke et al.,
    2017), and 'catboost' (Prokhorenkova et al., 2018
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1706.09516>) via 'reticulate' Python interoperability. Supports stochastic thinning
    spatial cross-validation, partial dependence plots, Accumulated Local
    Effects, and SHAP explainability.
